    "original_layout": {},
    "data": "DENGUE MANAGEMENT PROTOCOL (Version 3.1)\n\n1. Any patient presenting with C/O fever for 2-7 days should be tested for NS1 antigen.\n2. Platelet count below 20000 /uL requires admission to Ward 5 (Medicine).\n3. Paracetamol 650 mg every 6 hours; avoid NSAIDs.\n4. ASHA workers should follow up discharged patients on day 3.\n5. Differential diagnosis includes typhoid, malaria and, rarely, Addison's disease crisis.\n6. Dr. Ramesh Srivastava is the nodal officer.\n"
